-- title:
--   Kernel polynomial at p^k cuts out a cyclic subgroup of order p^k
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be an algebraically closed field, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $F$ which is elliptic (its discriminant is a unit), $p$ a prime with $p \neq 0$ in $F$, $k$ a natural number, and $h \in F[X]$. Assume [`ModularCurve.IsGamma0PowAt W p k h`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassGamma0Pow.html#L55), that is: if $p^k = 2$, then $h$ satisfies `W.IsTwoKernel`, i.e. $\deg h \le 1$, the coefficient of $h$ in degree $1$ equals $1$, and $h \mid W.\Psi_2^{\mathrm{Sq}}$; while if $p^k \neq 2$, then $h$ satisfies `W.IsCyclicGenKernel p k`, i.e. $\deg h \le \varphi(p^k)/2$, the coefficient of $h$ in degree $\varphi(p^k)/2$ equals $1$, one has $h \cdot W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi(p^{k-1}) \mid W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi(p^k)$, and $h \mid W.\mathrm{smulNumerator}\, a\, (\varphi(p^k)/2)\, h$ for every natural $a$ with $2 \le a \le (p^k-1)/2$ and $p \nmid a$. Let $S$ be the set of points of the affine model of $W$ of the form $(x,y)$ with $(x,y)$ nonsingular and $h(x) = 0$. The conclusion is that the additive subgroup of $W(F)$ generated by $S$ is cyclic and has cardinality exactly $p^k$.
--
--   This is the reading, over an algebraically closed base field in which $p$ is invertible, of a $\Gamma_0(p^k)$-structure given in kernel-polynomial form: the divisibility and scalar-stability conditions on $h$ force its roots to be the $x$-coordinates of the generators of a single cyclic subgroup of order $p^k$, recovered here as the subgroup generated by the affine points above the roots of $h$. It supplies the $\Gamma_0$ input to [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_levelReading_baseChange_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_levelReading_baseChange_of_isAlgClosed) and to its variant `ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_levelReading_baseChange_of_isAlgClosedRigidDataH1Pow`, where the explicit description of the subgroup makes its behaviour under base change along field automorphisms transparent.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IsGamma0PowAt_isAddCyclic_closure_and_natCard_eq_pow.lean

